; A cast into a struct another module keeps private still forges a
; reference. `Map` is private to `stdlib/Map.ax`, so its name is usable
; in this file's types while its constructor is not; the cast rule
; looked the struct up with this file's visibility, found nothing, and
; called the type unknown, so `(cast Map 4096)` checked in safe code
; and `mapLen` read word 0 of address 4096. It is AX3073 now, as a cast
; into a struct this file declares is.
(import Map)

(:: main ())
(fn (main)
  (mapLen (cast Map 4096)))
